Determination explanation: Utilization levels are mapped as below 50% = 0 levels, 50% to 70% = 1 range, 70% to 85% = 2 levels, 85% to 95% = 3 levels, and above 95% = 4 levels. This time, 62.4% is 1 level. There are only two conditions for capacity expansion to trigger: utilization reaches level 3 with neighboring area availability below 5%, or utilization reaches level 4; Tier 1 does not meet any of these requirements, so there is no need to arrange expansion. The order of action selection is: when expansion is triggered, prioritize the conditions for new site creation (only after 4 consecutive weeks of 4 levels and already filled units before creating a new site); if not triggered and the neighbor buffer exceeds 15%, you can choose off-streaming; if the buffer is sufficient and there is no sustained upward trend, keep watching; The balance in this single-neighbor area is 34.5%, with a historical three-week increase of less than 2 percentage points. Maintaining the status quo requires no action. Appendix: {device} version inspection is normal, {batch} spare parts have been stored in storage.

[Approval Remarks] {date} Capacity Action Approval Form {order_no}
Applicant: Transmission Engineer for a certain region; Target: {site} / {device}
Fact excerpt: Peak utilization during busy hours has remained stable at 85.2%–88.9% over the past 10 days. Take the highest value of 88.9%, and according to the slot rule, 85% (inclusive) to 95% (exclusive) is recorded in three tiers. Determination rules: Tier ≥3 is considered to require capacity expansion; The action priority is—Neighbor Zone/Neighbor Chain Peak ≤70%, and if offloading, then offload; If the peak value of neighboring zones/adjacent chains is >70% but the current slot or port allowance is ≥1, local expansion is required; If neither is met, then a new one is built. Verification conclusion: Peak value in adjacent areas is 91.2% (no diversion), {device} still has 1 idle slot (can be expanded locally), so it is approved to expand the capacity of the community at the existing station site and add one baseband board. Note: {batch} Batch will be reviewed by the duty staff upon arrival; Additionally, {ticket}'s air conditioning filter replacement for the data center was scheduled for the afternoon of {date} and does not conflict with this order.

